\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Clean non-identifiability witness}}{35}{figure.4.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Le Cam floor versus optimal committal regret}}{39}{figure.4.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Regret decomposition across policies}}{42}{figure.4.3}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces The batch certificate on the 123-task anomaly-routing suite (Chapter~\ref {ch:exp1}). Each point is one task: label-free estimated benefit $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \Delta $}\mathaccent "0362{\Delta }(Z)$ (horizontal) against the oracle true benefit (vertical), with the split-conformal band $\pm 0.049$ at $\alpha =0.1$ shaded around the ideal diagonal. Green points are certified \textsc {adapt}, red \textsc {freeze}, grey \textsc {abstain}: commitments concentrate where the certified interval clears zero, and abstentions cluster in the near-zero-benefit band where Theorem~\ref {thm:gate} prices commitment errors as cheap but Theorem~\ref {thm:cert} declines to make them.}}{52}{figure.5.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Suppression of harmful adaptation on the 123-task suite (produced by the knowability experiment of Chapter~\ref {ch:exp1}; same data as Figure~\ref {fig:t2-certificate}). Each bar is the fraction of adaptation decisions whose true benefit was negative: adapting always inherits the suite's harmful base rate $0.358$; a naive validation-threshold rule false-adapts on $0.180$ of its commitments; the certificate trichotomy on $0.100$ --- the complement of its $0.90$ adapt precision, in line with its calibrated level $\alpha =0.1$.}}{53}{figure.5.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces The level $\alpha $ as the safety--coverage dial, measured on the anomaly-routing benchmark of Chapter~\ref {ch:exp1} with the split-conformal batch certificate: $\alpha =0.01$ yields a $0\%$ observed false-adapt rate at $11\%$ coverage; $\alpha =0.1$ yields $0.065$ at $35\%$ coverage; $\alpha =0.2$ yields $0.072$ at $49\%$ coverage. The $\alpha =0.05$ point sits at $0.073$, slightly above its nominal budget --- an honest finite-sample fluctuation on $369$ instances under approximate cross-task exchangeability, and a reminder that the guarantee is marginal, not per-configuration.}}{57}{figure.5.3}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces \textsc {KGA}{} system architecture. Labelled calibration scores and an unlabelled test batch enter the pipeline. The label-free evidence $Z$ is computed first; then a finite-sample certificate $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \Delta $}\mathaccent "0362{\Delta }\pm \varepsilon $ is formed at level $\alpha $; finally the trichotomy maps the certificate to one of three actions. The adaptation mechanism (Tent, EATA, SAR, or any other) is a plug-in; \textsc {KGA}{} wraps it without modification. }}{69}{figure.6.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Decision flow for an incoming \texttt {POST /decide} request. Pydantic validates and coerces the inputs; \texttt {compute\_evidence} produces $Z$; \texttt {conformal\_split} builds $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \Delta $}\mathaccent "0362{\Delta }\pm \varepsilon $; and \texttt {decide} applies the trichotomy. Any \texttt {ValueError} from precondition checks (e.g., all-identical scores) is returned as \texttt {HTTP 400}; uncaught exceptions return \texttt {HTTP 500}. }}{78}{figure.6.2}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.1}{\ignorespaces \textsc {KGA}\ in the harmful-fusion regime. The certificate almost entirely blocks the legacy-fuse candidate; regret-to-oracle falls from $0.0214$ (always-adapt) to $0.0019$ (${\approx }11\times $ reduction). Source: \texttt {kbound\_harmful\_results.json}.}}{84}{figure.7.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.2}{\ignorespaces Mixed regime. \textbf {Left}: policy AUROC comparison---\textsc {KGA}\ beats always-freeze by $0.104$ and ties always-adapt. \textbf {Right}: \textsc {KGA}\ decision map by true condition---adapt concentrated on detectable-failure instances, abstain dominant on clean. Source: \texttt {mixed\_regime\_results.json}.}}{86}{figure.7.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.3}{\ignorespaces Evidence-component ablation: regret when each feature of $Z$ is removed. The \texttt {disagree} feature dominates: removing it raises regret $2.6\times $. Source: \texttt {ablations.json}.}}{89}{figure.7.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.4}{\ignorespaces Regression covariate shift: \textsc {KGA}\ matches always-freeze and the oracle (MSE $0.2513$) by refusing the harmful IW candidate on all 72 instances. Always-adapt (IW) reaches MSE $0.3376$. Source: \texttt {regression\_covariate.json}.}}{91}{figure.7.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.5}{\ignorespaces Regret-to-oracle across all sub-experiments of this chapter. \textsc {KGA}\ (blue) dominates always-adapt (orange) in the harmful and mixed regimes while remaining within range in the helpful regime. Always-freeze (grey) is safe only in harmful-dominated regimes. Source: aggregated from \texttt {knowability\_results.json}, \texttt {kbound\_harmful\_results.json}, \texttt {mixed\_regime\_results.json}, \texttt {rigor\_multiseed.json}, \texttt {regression\_covariate.json}.}}{94}{figure.7.5}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.1}{\ignorespaces Policy comparison on the CIFAR-10-C Tent stress grid (432 conditions). \textsc {KGA}{} (green) achieves higher mean accuracy than always-adapt while eliminating false adaptations; always-freeze pays large regret-to-oracle; the oracle is closely tracked by \textsc {KGA}{}. Source: \texttt {decisive\_tta\_results.json}.}}{99}{figure.8.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.2}{\ignorespaces CIFAR-10-C stress grid: regret-to-oracle vs.\ harmful fraction $p$ of the deployment stream, per candidate. \textsc {KGA}{} (green) stays on the Pareto front: ties always-adapt at $p{=}0$, strictly dominates both trivial policies at $p \geq p^\star $ (Tent/SAR: $p^\star {=}0.1$; EATA: $p^\star {=}0.0$), and never collapses. Source: \texttt {decisive\_tta\_results.json} (Pareto curves).}}{102}{figure.8.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.3}{\ignorespaces Left: regret-to-oracle per candidate/policy (lower is better). \textsc {KGA}{} reaches near-zero regret for all three candidates. Right: routing decisions by true regime --- adapt on helpful, freeze on harmful, abstain on marginal. Source: \texttt {decisive\_tta\_results.json}.}}{103}{figure.8.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.4}{\ignorespaces CIFAR-10-C per-corruption suite. \emph {Left}: severity-5 accuracy by corruption type --- online Tent and \textsc {KGA}{} both recover over the frozen baseline; no per-corruption collapse is observed. \emph {Right}: knowability crossover map --- adaptation headroom (oracle gain over frozen) by corruption $\times $ severity; headroom is large on noise/blur corruptions and small on easier corruptions such as brightness, matching where the true benefit $\Delta $ is large. Source: \texttt {cifar10c\_suite\_results.json}.}}{104}{figure.8.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.5}{\ignorespaces Per-window accuracy on the \emph {harm-dominated} non-stationary stream (pink shading $=$ catastrophic ``trap'' windows). Continual Tent (always-adapt) accumulates damage through the long trap runs and collapses; \textsc {KGA}{} freezes or abstains on trap windows and never collapses, staying near always-freeze while capturing gains in recoverable windows. Source: \texttt {cifar\_tent\_online\_results.json}.}}{105}{figure.8.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.6}{\ignorespaces TTA collapse regime: \textsc {KGA}{} decision pattern on the collapse benchmark (\texttt {tta\_collapse\_results.json}). In the pure-harmful task set (210 conditions) \textsc {KGA}{} correctly freezes or abstains everywhere, making 0 false-adapt decisions (adapt-precision $1.0$, false-adapt $0.0$).}}{106}{figure.8.6}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.1}{\ignorespaces The bounded-drift knowability boundary (Proposition~\ref {thm:reg-iff}). Left: the decision target $\Delta $ is invariant to unknown label noise while cardinal risks are confounded (Proposition~\ref {thm:reg-noise}). Right: identifiability holds exactly while the observable margin $|U-2T_S|$ exceeds the tight drift reach $2BW$; the crossing defines the computable boundary $B^\star $.}}{158}{figure.C.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.2}{\ignorespaces The label-shift boundary (Proposition~\ref {thm:ls-iff}). Left: injective evidence operator, reach $0$ --- always identifiable. Right: singular evidence; the benefit $\Delta (\pi +tv)$ sweeps the reach interval along the unobservable null segment and crosses zero --- identifiable exactly when the margin clears the reach.}}{161}{figure.C.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.3}{\ignorespaces One quantity decides every family (Proposition~\ref {thm:unify}): identifiable iff the margin $|c|$ exceeds the reach $\rho $. Bars: closed forms; diamonds: brute-force empirical reach over admissible equivalent worlds.}}{162}{figure.C.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.4}{\ignorespaces Multi-candidate identifiability (Proposition~\ref {thm:multicand}, Proposition~\ref {prop:cei-test}). Left: the label-free ordering estimator is exact under conditional error-independence and degrades as it fails. Right: the overdetermination residual is a checkable diagnostic --- $\approx \!0$ under independence, rising with error-correlation.}}{166}{figure.C.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.5}{\ignorespaces The $\gamma $-meter and the agreement-invisible reach. Left: $|\hat \gamma -\gamma |$ decays at the proven $n^{-1/2}$ rate (Theorem~\ref {thm:gmeter}). Right: the constructive invisible reach $t_{\max }$ (closed form) versus the exact LP reach over all pairwise-agreement-preserving couplings; the LP reach does not shrink with $M$ --- only richer (third-order) evidence shrinks it (Proposition~\ref {prop:third-order}).}}{173}{figure.C.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.6}{\ignorespaces The knowability frontier (Proposition~\ref {prop:kfrontier}). Left: synthetic stream with planted ambiguous mass --- false-adapt stays below $\alpha $, coverage dominates the $\mathbb {P}[\kappa _\alpha >0]-\alpha $ bound, and commits on ambiguous evidence respect the $2\alpha $ converse cap. Right: the same certificate on the \emph {real} 123-task archive. Produced by \texttt {scripts/knowability\_frontier\_validation.py}.}}{174}{figure.C.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.7}{\ignorespaces Prior decision styles as degenerate certificates (Propositions~\ref {prop:s1}--\ref {prop:s2}). Left: always-adapt pays the full false-adapt regret mass; the certificate's committal regret is zero. Right: in a confidently-wrong world an entropy/confidence filter adapts blindly while the certificate holds $\mathrm {FA}\le \alpha $.}}{176}{figure.C.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.8}{\ignorespaces The knowability rate (Propositions~\ref {thm:rate-ub}--\ref {thm:rate-lb}). Achieved certifiable margin of the deployed empirical-Bernstein certificate versus the two-point lower bound, in the dense ($n^{-1/2}$) and spike ($n^{-1}$) regimes; slopes match and the offset is a bounded universal constant.}}{178}{figure.C.8}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.9}{\ignorespaces The one-bit theorem, validated. Left (Thm~\ref {thm:flip-witness}): the flip witness $P'$ matches the full evidence law of $P$ (TV $=0$; identical agreement products) while every advantage and benefit sign is negated. Right (Thm~\ref {thm:onebit-id}): label-free recovery of $b$ up to the bit at the $m^{-1/2}$ rate (log-log slope $-0.51$).}}{181}{figure.C.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.10}{\ignorespaces The budget audit (Thms~\ref {thm:audit},~\ref {thm:no-verify}). Sound at level $\alpha $ under a true budget; power $1.000$ against violations beyond the radius (bootstrap); correctly blind on the bit-ambiguous set $\mathcal B_\beta $ and on the rank-one-preserving stealth law ($\tau \approx 0$) --- the two provably irreducible blind zones; $\tau $ rises with overt error-correlation $\rho $ (Pearson $0.914$).}}{182}{figure.C.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.11}{\ignorespaces The evidence-channel rate (Thm~\ref {thm:ev-rate}). Empirical minimax error tracks the Le Cam curve $c_0/\sqrt m$ (slope $-0.525$); per-sample KL grows quadratically in the separation (KL$/\varepsilon ^2$ constant); the labeled-vs-evidence efficiency ratio is constant in $m$ but grows as $c_{\min }\to 0$.}}{184}{figure.C.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.12}{\ignorespaces Closing Conjecture~\ref {conj:gen} (Thm~\ref {thm:conj1-dichotomy}): the swap flips every benefit sign (multiclass $K{=}5$, left; regression, middle) while no label-free observable of any order moves (right, exact zero) --- so no testable assumption can bracket the sign, and the residual is exactly one bit.}}{186}{figure.C.12}%
